    "rich-text": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "How It All Began"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "enlarge_text": false,
            "text": "<h2><strong>How It All Began</strong></h2><h3><strong>Filling a Void for Barre, Pilates & Yoga</strong></h3><p>As a longtime fan and practitioner of Barre, I was literally unable to <em>“get a grip”</em> during my practice. Movement was my ritual—my space for strength, focus, and connection—but class after class, something kept breaking that flow.</p><p>At the time, <strong>grippy yoga socks were the only tool available</strong>. Instead of supporting movement, they consistently disrupted it. They slipped when grip mattered most, required constant adjusting mid-exercise, and never delivered the control they promised. I found myself breaking focus to fix socks instead of holding positions, sliding out of side planks and losing stability where it mattered most. Over time, they also trapped sweat, becoming uncomfortable and unsanitary—<strong>bacteria magnets that diminished the practice rather than enhanced it</strong>.</p><p>One day, stuck in side plank and sliding yet again, it became clear: <strong>this wasn’t just inconvenient—it was holding us back.</strong></p><p>That moment sparked a question: <em>Why didn’t a better tool exist?</em></p><h3><strong>The Idea</strong></h3><p>What if there were a flexible, non-slip, in-studio workout shoe with <strong>true all-over grip</strong>—something that could move seamlessly from side plank to flat-back chair without slipping, shifting, or interrupting flow?</p><p>That same evening, I tore the silicone sleeve off a water bottle, cut it up, and created my very first prototype.</p><p>From that moment on, <strong>Barre + Pilates + Yoga workout footwear changed.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "26f5e414-b901-45f1-974f-f5b0ed008699": {
          "type": "heading",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Trial and Error"
          }
        },
        "943ed80a-f31f-478b-a65b-99ecc46b9237": {
          "type": "text",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "enlarge_text": false,
            "text": "<p>Two years and multiple iterations later,that wild idea and on-the-fly prototype has been thoroughly researched,developed and produced, honing <br/>pressure points, fit and a patented materiality. </p><p>The <strong>barreletics</strong> performance<br/> skin is the only Barre-specific footwear on the market, and our team <br/>soon recognized the versatility. The design is equally adapted to yoga, <br/>pilates, boxing, <br/>water sports and more. One of my favorite uses of the shoe is for stand-up paddle boarding!</p>"
          }
        },
