        "text_VD4dQp": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>At the time, grippy yoga socks were the only tool available. </strong>Instead of supporting my workout, they consistently disrupted it. They slipped when grip mattered most, required constant adjusting mid-exercise, and never delivered the control they promised.<br/><br/></p><p>I found myself breaking focus to fix my socks instead of holding positions, sliding out of side planks, resetting my feet, and losing stability where it mattered most.<br/><br/></p><p>Over time, they also trapped sweat and felt like bacteria magnets — uncomfortable, unsanitary, and completely misaligned with the clean, connected experience I wanted in my practice.</p><p>What seemed like a small annoyance became impossible to ignore.<br/><br/></p><p>I was investing time, energy, commitment, and resources into my workout without having the right tool to fully support it. If I was dedicating an hour to my practice, I wanted that hour to count. I wanted to feel secure, grounded, connected, and confident — not distracted by what was happening beneath my feet.<br/><br/></p><p><strong>And I knew I was not the only one.</strong></p>",
            "text_custom": false,
            "text_font": "josefin_sans_n4",
            "text_size": 16,
            "text_size_mobile": 16,
            "text_height": 150,
            "text_mt": 16,
            "text_mt_mobile": 12,
            "text_color": "#121212"
          }
        }
      },
